Fix FTBFS on Linux 7.2+: the cpuid_*() helpers moved out of <asm/processor.h>
into <asm/cpuid/api.h>, so zenpower_core.c calls cpuid_ecx() with no
declaration and -Werror=implicit-function-declaration rejects the build.

__has_include instead of a LINUX_VERSION_CODE gate: distributions backport the
header move, so the version number is not a reliable proxy for where the
declaration lives.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/mattkeenan/zenpower5/issues/13
Upstream PR:    https://github.com/mattkeenan/zenpower5/pull/16 (open, unmerged)

Drop this patch when upstream ships its own fix. The diff context spans the
insertion point both candidate fixes use, so the patch stops applying -- and
the build fails loudly -- the moment upstream lands one.

--- a/zenpower_core.c
+++ b/zenpower_core.c
@@ -46,6 +46,18 @@
 #include <asm/amd_nb.h>
 #endif
 
+#ifdef __has_include
+#if __has_include(<asm/cpuid/api.h>)
+#include <asm/cpuid/api.h>
+#elif __has_include(<asm/cpuid.h>)
+#include <asm/cpuid.h>
+#else
+#include <asm/processor.h>
+#endif
+#else
+#include <asm/processor.h>
+#endif
+
 #include "zenpower.h"
 
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 14, 0) /* asm/amd_node.h */
